     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Hello,<br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">I&#39;m learning r-inla syntax. It is possible to infer the parameters alpha, beta, and gamma for the model defined below? </span>Thanks!<span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span>1<span style=\"color:#000\"><br>beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><code><span style=\"color:#066\">0.001</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>delta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rpois</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">lambda</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> exp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">arima</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">delta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y2 + rnorm(length(t))<br>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>I was trying something along the lines of</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inla</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> f</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;ar1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> f</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">copy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;exponential&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> copy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            family </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gaussian&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            control</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">link</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;identity&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><div>but I&#39;m not sure if that makes sense at all.<br></div></div>"
    ]
